,"isOpenAccess":"N","inEPMC":"Y","inPMC":"Y","citedByCount":18,"hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"Y","dbCrossReferenceList":{"dbName":["INTERPRO"]},"hasPDF":"Y","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"N","hasLabsLinks":"Y","hasData":"Y","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"Y","tmAccessionTypeList":{"accessionType":["gen","uniprot","pdb"]},"dateOfCompletion":"2020-06-08","dateOfCreation":"2019-08-14","dateOfRevision":"2024-07-20","electronicPublicationDate":"2019-10-04","firstPublicationDate":"2019-10-04","firstIndexDate":"2019-08-14","fullTextReceivedDate":"2025-02-04","embargoDate":"2020-04-04","hasEvaluations":"N"},{"id":"35176283","source":"MED","pmid":"35176283","pmcid":"PMC8958531","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC8958531"]},"doi":"10.1016/j.jbc.2022.101733","title":"Contrasting roles for two conserved arginines: Stabilizing flavin semiquinone or quaternary structure, in bifurcating electron transfer flavoproteins.","authorString":"Mohamed-Raseek N, Miller AF.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Mohamed-Raseek N","lastName":"Mohamed-Raseek","firstName":"Nishya","initials":"N","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-5086-1410"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Chemistry, University of Kentucky, Lexington, Kentucky, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Miller AF","lastName":"Miller","firstName":"Anne-Frances","initials":"AF","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Chemistry, University of Kentucky, Lexington, Kentucky, USA. Electronic address: afmill3r2@gmail.com."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-5086-1410"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-7497-5631"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"4","volume":"298","journalIssueId":3337770,"dateOfPublication":"2022 Apr","monthOfPublication":4,"yearOfPublication":2022,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"J Biol Chem","title":"The Journal of biological chemistry","essn":"1083-351X","issn":"0021-9258","isoabbreviation":"J Biol Chem","nlmid":"2985121R"},"printPublicationDate":"2022-04-01"},"pubYear":"2022","pageInfo":"101733","abstractText":"Bifurcating electron transfer flavoproteins (Bf ETFs) are important redox enzymes that contain two flavin adenine dinucleotide (FAD) cofactors, with contrasting reactivities and complementary roles in electron bifurcation. However, for both the \"electron transfer\" (ET) and the \"bifurcating\" (Bf) FADs, the only charged amino acid within 5 Å of the flavin is a conserved arginine (Arg) residue. To understand how the two sites produce different reactivities utilizing the same residue, we investigated the consequences of replacing each of the Arg residues with lysine, glutamine, histidine, or alanine. We show that absence of a positive charge in the ET site diminishes accumulation of the anionic semiquinone (ASQ) that enables the ET flavin to act as a single electron carrier, due to depression of the oxidized versus. ASQ reduction midpoint potential, E°<sub>OX/ASQ</sub>. Perturbation of the ET site also affected the remote Bf site, whereas abrogation of Bf FAD binding accelerated chemical modification of the ET flavin. In the Bf site, removal of the positive charge impaired binding of FAD or AMP, resulting in unstable protein. Based on pH dependence, we propose that the Bf site Arg interacts with the phosphate(s) of Bf FAD or AMP, bridging the domain interface via a conserved peptide loop (\"zipper\") and favoring nucleotide binding. We further propose a model that rationalizes conservation of the Bf site Arg even in non-Bf ETFs, as well as AMP's stabilizing role in the latter, and provides a mechanism for coupling Bf flavin redox changes to domain-scale motion.","affiliation":"Department of Chemistry, University of Kentucky, Lexington, Kentucky, USA.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"National Science Foundation","grantId":"CLP-2108134","orderIn":0},{"agency":"National Science Foundation","grantId":"CLP-1808433","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Flavin-Adenine Dinucleotide","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"AA","qualifierName":"analogs & derivatives"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Electron-Transferring Flavoproteins","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Flavins","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Arginine","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Adenosine Monophosphate","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Electron Transport"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Oxidation-Reduction"}]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["Site-directed mutagenesis","Energy efficiency","Conformational change","Electron transfer","flavoprotein","Flavin","Electron Bifurcation","Domain Interface","Flavin Adenine Dinucleotide (Fad)","Redox Tuning"]},"chemicalList":{"chemical":[{"name":"flavin semiquinone","registryNumber":"35919-91-6"},{"name":"Flavin-Adenine Dinucleotide","registryNumber":"146-14-5"},{"name":"Flavins","registryNumber":"0"},{"name":"Electron-Transferring Flavoproteins","registryNumber":"0"},{"name":"Adenosine Monophosphate","registryNumber":"415SHH325A"},{"name":"Arginine","registryNumber":"94ZLA3W45F"}]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jbc.2022.101733"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"html","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC8958531"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC8958531?pdf=render"}]},"isOpenAccess":"Y","inEPMC":"Y","inPMC":"Y","citedByCount":14,"hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"Y","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"Y","hasLabsLinks":"Y","hasData":"Y","license":"cc by-nc-nd","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"Y","tmAccessionTypeList":{"accessionType":["pdb"]},"dateOfCompletion":"2022-04-26","dateOfCreation":"2022-02-17","dateOfRevision":"2023-07-12","electronicPublicationDate":"2022-02-15","firstPublicationDate":"2022-02-15","firstIndexDate":"2022-02-18","fullTextReceivedDate":"2022-04-11","hasEvaluations":"N"},{"id":"23772070","source":"MED","pmid":"23772070","pmcid":"PMC3754583","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC3754583"]},"doi":"10.1128/jb.00321-13","title":"Effect of an oxygen-tolerant bifurcating butyryl coenzyme A dehydrogenase/electron-transferring flavoprotein complex from Clostridium difficile on butyrate production in Escherichia coli.","authorString":"Aboulnaga el-H, Pinkenburg O, Schiffels J, El-Refai A, Buckel W, Selmer T.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Aboulnaga el-H","lastName":"Aboulnaga","firstName":"El-Hussiny","initials":"el-H","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Aachen University of Applied Sciences, Campus Juelich, Department of Chemistry and Biotechnology, Juelich, Germany."}]}},{"fullName":"Pinkenburg O","lastName":"Pinkenburg","firstName":"Olaf","initials":"O"},{"fullName":"Schiffels J","lastName":"Schiffels","firstName":"Johannes","initials":"J","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-9674-9339"}},{"fullName":"El-Refai A","lastName":"El-Refai","firstName":"Ahmed","initials":"A"},{"fullName":"Buckel W","lastName":"Buckel","firstName":"Wolfgang","initials":"W"},{"fullName":"Selmer T","lastName":"Selmer","firstName":"Thorsten","initials":"T"}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-9674-9339"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"16","volume":"195","journalIssueId":2059952,"dateOfPublication":"2013 Aug","monthOfPublication":8,"yearOfPublication":2013,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"J Bacteriol","title":"Journal of bacteriology","essn":"1098-5530","issn":"0021-9193","isoabbreviation":"J Bacteriol","nlmid":"2985120R"},"printPublicationDate":"2013-08-01"},"pubYear":"2013","pageInfo":"3704-3713","abstractText":"The butyrogenic genes from Clostridium difficile DSM 1296(T) have been cloned and expressed in Escherichia coli. The enzymes acetyl-coenzyme A (CoA) C-acetyltransferase, 3-hydroxybutyryl-CoA dehydrogenase, crotonase, phosphate butyryltransferase, and butyrate kinase and the butyryl-CoA dehydrogenase complex composed of the dehydrogenase and two electron-transferring flavoprotein subunits were individually produced in E. coli and kinetically characterized in vitro. While most of these enzymes were measured using well-established test systems, novel methods to determine butyrate kinase and butyryl-CoA dehydrogenase activities with respect to physiological function were developed. Subsequently, the individual genes were combined to form a single plasmid-encoded operon in a plasmid vector, which was successfully used to confer butyrate-forming capability to the host. In vitro and in vivo studies demonstrated that C. difficile possesses a bifurcating butyryl-CoA dehydrogenase which catalyzes the NADH-dependent reduction of ferredoxin coupled to the reduction of crotonyl-CoA also by NADH. Since the reoxidation of ferredoxin by a membrane-bound ferredoxin:NAD(+)-oxidoreductase enables electron transport phosphorylation, additional ATP is formed. The butyryl-CoA dehydrogenase from C. difficile is oxygen stable and apparently uses oxygen as a co-oxidant of NADH in the presence of air. These properties suggest that this enzyme complex might be well suited to provide butyryl-CoA for solventogenesis in recombinant strains. The central role of bifurcating butyryl-CoA dehydrogenases and membrane-bound ferredoxin:NAD oxidoreductases (Rhodobacter nitrogen fixation [RNF]), which affect the energy yield of butyrate fermentation in the clostridial metabolism, is discussed.","affiliation":"Aachen University of Applied Sciences, Campus Juelich, Department of Chemistry and Biotechnology, Juelich, Germany.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","research-article","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Escherichia coli","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Oxygen"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Butyrates","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Electron-Transferring Flavoproteins","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","